  "id": "fbc62b34-72ed-5b9b-843c-c38054af0e18",
  "slug": "easy-fermented-pickled-veggies-recipe-8658149",
  "name": "Easy Fermented Pickled Veggies",
  "recipe_type": "salad",
  "brief_description": "These easy fermented pickled veggies, or refrigerator pickles, are great for your gut, and they add funky flavor and crunch to salads, sandwiches, and snack plates.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To sanitize jar, put a 1-quart wide-mouthed canning jar in a 6- to 8-quart pot; cover with tap water. (You could also use multiple smaller wide-mouthed canning jars.) Bring to a boil; boil 10 minutes. Using tongs, carefully remove jar from pot, draining excess water; let jar cool slightly. Meanwhile, for brine, stir together filtered water and salt in a 1-quart measuring cup until salt is dissolved."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add radishes (or other VEGETABLES), mint (or other HERBS), peppercorns (or other KICK), and garlic to jar. Veggies can be packed tightly; they will shrink and soften as they pickle. Fill jar with brine; you may have brine left over. Add a fermenting weight or an inverted, sanitized plastic lid to keep vegetables submerged."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Cover jar with a kitchen towel, securing with a rubber band. Let stand at room temperature for at least 24 hours or up to 3 days. You\u2019ll start to see bubbles forming. The vegetables will become more tart and the brine will become cloudier the longer the pickles stand. Remove fermenting weight and screw on metal lid. Chill up to 3 weeks."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 16,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
  "difficulty": "easy",
